+++ b/typescript/.changeset/bazaar-schema-validation-no-codegen.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+---
+"@x402/extensions": patch
+---
+
+Extension schema validation no longer generates code at runtime. `validateDiscoveryExtension` (Bazaar), `validatePaymentIdentifier` and `validateErc20ApprovalGasSponsoringInfo` previously built an Ajv instance and compiled their schema on every call; Ajv's `compile` uses `new Function()`, which Cloudflare Workers forbid during request handling, so on workerd every valid Bazaar or payment-identifier extension was reported as `valid: false` ("Code generation from strings disallowed for this context"), `validateErc20ApprovalGasSponsoringInfo` threw an uncaught `EvalError`, and each request paid for a failed compile. All three now share one interpreting validator (`@cfworker/json-schema`), run identically on Node, bundlers and Workers, and have no per-call compilation step. `ajv` is no longer a dependency of this package.
+
+Compatibility notes: `format` keywords stay annotation-only by default, as before; `validateDiscoveryExtension` accepts `{ assertFormats: true }` to enforce well-known formats (`uri`, `date-time`, `email`, `uuid`, ...). A non-object `schema`, a `$schema` other than JSON Schema 2020-12, and an external `$ref`/`$id` (now also for payment-identifier schemas) are rejected with explicit errors instead of failing at compile time. Fractional `multipleOf` divisors are compared with a small tolerance (0.3 is accepted as a multiple of 0.1), where the previous implementation compared the raw floating-point quotient and rejected such pairs. Validation error wording has changed.
